      "locations": [
        {
          "file": "orders_api/cache.py",
          "symbol": "OrderCache.remember",
          "line": 41,
          "excerpt": "def remember(self, order_id: str, payload: bytes) -> None:\n    self._held[order_id] = payload\n    self._held_mb += len(payload) / 1_048_576\n    log.warning(\"order cache grew\", extra={\"held_mb\": self._held_mb})",
          "why": "writes into a plain dict with no eviction; the log line matches the 'order cache grew' WARNING seen 76 times before the kill"
        },
        {
          "file": "orders_api/worker.py",
          "symbol": "leak_loop",
          "line": 18,
          "excerpt": "while True:\n    cache.remember(uuid4().hex, bytearray(STEP_MB * 1_048_576))\n    time.sleep(INTERVAL_S)",
          "why": "calls remember() every INTERVAL_S seconds with STEP_MB of fresh bytes, which matches the 20 MB per 5 s growth in the leak profile"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "OrderCache.remember stores every payload in a dict that is never trimmed, and leak_loop feeds it 20 MB every 5 seconds. Resident memory therefore grows without bound until the kernel kills the process, exactly as the triage leak profile shows.",
      "developer_action": "Bound OrderCache with an LRU (maxsize or max_bytes) and evict in remember(); add a unit test that asserts held_mb stays under the limit after 10,000 inserts.",
      "recent_commits": [
        {"sha": "a1f3c9e", "date": "2026-11-12", "message": "cache: keep full order payload for replay", "files": ["orders_api/cache.py"]},
